<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "mover.dashboard">
<!ENTITY author    "RapidMark">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.11.26">
<!ENTITY md5       "e2d230303213a031a0377031100c7c06">
<!ENTITY sha256    "d843ee585971514df65fd6f962a120754b106fbdda7c654a1ce928c51e85f3d4">
<!ENTITY github    "RapidMark/unraid-mover-dashboard">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY packageURL "https://github.com/&github;/releases/download/&version;/&name;-&version;.txz">
<!ENTITY flash     "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY plugdir   "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" launch="Mover" icon="truck" min="7.0.0" support="https://github.com/&github;/issues">

<CHANGES>
###2026.11.26
- A very long file name no longer pushes the percentage and target drive out of the Moving now panel; the name is shortened with an ellipsis.

###2026.11.24
- Keeps its state in /var/run instead of /tmp (suggested by the Community Applications review).
- The package is also checked by SHA256.
- No fonts are loaded from Google; the page uses local fonts.

###2026.11.23
- The Plugins page shows the name Mover Dashboard instead of mover.dashboard.

###2026.11.20
- First release: a Mover tab with the file being moved and its progress, the mover's queue, what is waiting on each cache pool, read and write per drive with the apps using them, and array write speed over 15 minutes.
</CHANGES>

<!-- Old versions left on the flash drive. -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
mkdir -p "&flash;"
find "&flash;" -maxdepth 1 -name '&name;-*.txz' ! -name '&name;-&version;.txz' -delete 2>/dev/null
true
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&flash;/&name;-&version;.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>&packageURL;</URL>
<MD5>&md5;</MD5>
<SHA256>&sha256;</SHA256>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
# State moved to /var/run in 2026.11.24.
rm -rf /tmp/&name;
echo "&name; &version; installed. Open the Mover tab."
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
removepkg "&name;-&version;" 2>/dev/null
rm -rf "&plugdir;" "&flash;" /var/run/&name; /tmp/&name;
echo "&name; removed."
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
